[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3661264992","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114078#issuecomment-3661264992","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114078","id":3661264992,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aOnhg","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T15:58:44Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T15:58:44Z","body":"That's not really a bug I'd say. When you attach a script, the script becomes the edited object. So panels like the inspector or signals pane will show you the properties and signals of the script (which is a resource) instead of the node. When you click the node afterwards the node becomes the edited object again.\n\nMight be worth reconsidering this behaviour though. Usually a script does not have relevant ways to interact with through the inspector. So keeping the node the edited object when attaching a script might be a better choice.\n\nBefore https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101787 signals and groups were part of the \"Node\" dock which only worked for Nodes which is why it was empty when the Script resource was the edited object.\n\nWhat I don't know is whether the panel is intended to work with resources after the split, or if this is a regression from the above mentioned PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3661264992/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3701850768","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114078#issuecomment-3701850768","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114078","id":3701850768,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7cpcKQ","user":{"login":"OlegVegan","id":9021673,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMjE2NzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9021673?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan","html_url":"https://github.com/OlegVegan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OlegVegan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-31T09:45:49Z","updated_at":"2025-12-31T09:45:49Z","body":"I often attach scripts to then connect them with a signal right away (you can't do it without having a script), so whenever they disappear like that, it does feel like a usability bug. I can't think of any situation where the current behavior is useful ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3701850768/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]